
# KRAM server passcode - never commit
api-server/.kram-server-bran.txt

# Hosting-readiness fix: task-data/ holds every agent's BRAN file (the KERI
# private-key-equivalent passcode) plus derived identity/credential info.
# This was NOT excluded before - if this repo is ever pushed to a remote,
# every agent's private key material would be committed. Excluding the whole
# directory (not just *.txt) because the *-info.json / *-credential-info.json
# files derived from those BRANs are also sensitive KERI state, not just the
# raw passcodes.
#
# NOTE: if task-data/ is already tracked by git in this repo, adding it here
# only stops FUTURE commits - it does NOT remove it from existing git history.
# Run `git ls-files task-data` to check; if any files are listed, the BRANs
# in git history must be treated as compromised (rotate/regenerate identities)
# and the history itself scrubbed (git filter-repo or equivalent) separately.
task-data/

# 2026-11-13: run logs may contain secrets from older runs; local edit backups
*-run.log
4d-run.log
.edit-backup-*/

# 2026-11-13 (vLEI-3.4 Phase B): per-request invoice configs generated by the Signatory runner
appconfig/generated-runs/
